<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of running verse, set in italic; running head at top; catchword "Sed" at lower right. No margin notes.</layout>
  <page_number>24</page_number>
  <running_head>IBERICA,</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Sed</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Non vllius cita trabis celerrima</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Praeteruolabit hunc fuga.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Nam seu volandum est palmulis; seu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>linteo, Nec linteo, nec palmulis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Potis est Draconis vlla nauem consequi,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Nec vim Draconis fallere.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Testatur hoc sinus minoris Adriæ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Testantur hoc &amp; Cyclades.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Euxini Neptune, &amp; Tomitani salis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Neptune, tibi isthæc nota sunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Nosces Draconem, Hispane, nosces</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Anglicos Animos, &amp; invictas manus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Debes Philippe damna, luctum patriæ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Ludibrium vento &amp; mari.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>En fortis urget te Draco, invictum tibi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>En obiicit robur virum:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Te te catenis illigabit, te Draco</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Damnabit atro carcere.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Pars, esca piscium voracium, breui</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Natabis imo gurgite.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Pars præda mergis es futura hiantibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Eiecta curuo in litore.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Quæ tu minatus es Britannis vincula,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Hæc ipse vinctus indues.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Quid ora tot rostrata ducis navium,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Seruus futurus hostium?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Ut vela das retrò! ut fugam capessis! ut</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Pugna timidè dilaberis!</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed "Ani:nos" in the line "Animos, &amp; invictas manus" shows a stray mark between "Ani" and "nos"; copied as printed with the colon. The word at the end of "Hæc ipse vinctus indues" is set with a ligature and may read differently. The text is set in italic throughout; the long s is rendered as s. No margin notes, and no reference marks in the text.</notes>
</page>
